WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:03.710
- [Guy] I think I've just
held on to so much pain

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:08.260
and so much anger and
shame over so many things

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.413
that are ultimately I
shouldn't be ashamed of.

00:00:11.713 --> 00:00:14.950
(upbeat inspirational music)

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.760
- Three, two, one, break.

00:00:17.683 --> 00:00:20.433
(glass shatters)

00:00:20.673 --> 00:00:24.610
(fast-paced instrumental music)

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.030
- I'm Diego Torres Caso.

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:26.920
- Hi, my name's Darren.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:28.173
- My name is Brenden.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:29.243
- I'm a little nervous.

00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:31.290
I honestly don't do much in
front of the camera stuff.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.780
I'm typically behind the camera.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:36.280
I hope to overcome the idea
of letting others' opinions

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:37.830
stop me from doing things.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:42.000
- If one person can benefit
from me putting myself out there

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:45.650
and sharing, even if that
one person is only myself,

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.970
and this just helps me
heal a little bit more

00:00:47.971 --> 00:00:49.163
then I'm okay.

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:51.270
- I hope it'll put me on a fresh page

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:54.173
before I start college
with some more confidence.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.820
- My name is Maxwell Poth
and we are here today

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.497
working with queer youth

00:00:58.497 --> 00:01:00.470
and we're gonna be photographing them

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:02.510
and creating a beautiful project.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:04.670
Project Contrast is my photo project

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:06.760
that I've now turned into a non-profit.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.820
I created Project Contrast
to prevent suicide rates

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:12.720
in the LGBTQ youth community.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:14.510
And we're giving them
the opportunity to become

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.940
the advocates that they wanna be

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.080
but they just don't have
the platform for it.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.810
There are youth all over this country

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.838
who feel alone and afraid of who they are

00:01:21.838 --> 00:01:23.950
and a lot of them end
up taking their lives.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.353
They're just gonna leave
hopefully empowered.

00:01:28.030 --> 00:01:30.800
- For me, a lot of my
insecurities surround

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.720
my struggle with gender identity disorder.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.550
My voice, my it's tough
to talk about you know,

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:39.230
like for me those aspects of my body

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:42.503
just seem toxic and unhomely to me.

00:01:43.130 --> 00:01:45.020
- Being in front of the camera, you know,

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:47.000
and having dealt with
like an eating disorder

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:51.663
and just not feeling a lot of worth,

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.233
it was difficult.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.600
- My biggest insecurity
is definitely my skin.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.830
But it's like my biggest
insecurity due to the way

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:01.710
that like, other people
perceive me based off that.

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.050
And a lot of that though is just me

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.500
being insecure within myself.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.270
Because like, maybe they're
not judging me for it.

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.173
But like, it eats me alive that like,

00:02:08.270 --> 00:02:10.370
the thought that they
are judging me for it.

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.830
- Something I think is
helpful to cope with that,

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:14.410
is think of your friends.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:17.380
Like, some of them definitely
have acne, you know?

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.950
But do you know which ones?

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.023
Like, I don't.

00:02:20.445 --> 00:02:21.278
I don't remember.

00:02:21.278 --> 00:02:22.700
- I will make a mistake
on somebody and be like,

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.870
oh my gosh, I'm so stupid.

00:02:23.870 --> 00:02:26.010
But like, even though
it's just like a word

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:27.240
and like I just like kinda write it off

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:28.270
and like, say it so often,

00:02:28.270 --> 00:02:30.110
like, that word actually
has like, meaning to it.

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.520
By doing that, like, I
feel like you almost like,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.070
internalize it and start to believe it.

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.060
Instead of like, bringing each other up,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.110
or like bringing yourself up,

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:40.133
like, we're kind of constantly
like, tearing ourselves down.

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.613
- Even if it's directed
towards someone else,

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.320
it's just eating away at you

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.733
and your mood or positivity.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:50.960
- Why are we so careful about
how we talk about other people

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:52.930
but we don't do the same with ourselves?

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.310
- [Diego] I wanna let go of the idea

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:57.810
that my identity is a
disappointment to someone.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.770
And that I am letting people down

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:03.920
by expressing who I truly am.

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.803
- [Brenden] Constantly
feeling like I'm broken.

00:03:07.130 --> 00:03:11.003
- [Darren] My voice, my fat distribution,

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:14.130
my sex characteristics, my height even.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.080
- [Diego] It's something
that I really battle with,

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.420
the idea that like, I
can't have a relationship

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:21.190
or I can't be vulnerable with people

00:03:21.190 --> 00:03:23.870
because that would require
me to be too honest.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:27.363
- [Darren] I want to channel
that I don't care attitude.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.100
And really let go of all the things

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.040
that have been bothering me.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.100
- [Diego] I stop myself
doing certain things

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.120
because of the idea
that it'll be perceived

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.880
as me being too feminine.

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:39.033
As if being feminine is a bad thing.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:42.823
- Just after today, I just
want to keep moving forward.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:45.103
Because I'm not broken.

00:03:45.546 --> 00:03:47.203
I'm not crazy.

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:52.013
Because at the end of the
day, I am a human being.

00:03:52.368 --> 00:03:53.737
(upbeat soft music)

00:03:53.737 --> 00:03:55.563
(glass shatters)

00:03:55.563 --> 00:03:58.563
(upbeat soft music)

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:03.313
- Holy...

00:04:03.769 --> 00:04:04.602
(guys laugh)

00:04:04.602 --> 00:04:07.602
(upbeat soft music)

00:04:12.502 --> 00:04:16.874
- [Maxwell] Who do you see
when you look into that photo?

00:04:16.874 --> 00:04:17.932
(slow serene music)

00:04:17.932 --> 00:04:18.765
- I don't know.

00:04:18.765 --> 00:04:19.598
(laughs)

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:20.723
It's like,

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.800
I see someone who's like,
strong and typically I don't

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:28.030
perceive myself like that
so it's definitely something

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.790
that I want to start looking

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:31.370
in the mirror and seeing
someone strong as well.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.320
I want to look in the
mirror and see someone

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.460
who looks like that every single
time I look in the mirror.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:37.490
- It's new, it's different and it's a side

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:40.210
that I didn't really think other people

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:41.860
would like, get to see like that.

00:04:41.930 --> 00:04:44.113
- It was just so therapeutic today.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:49.370
To just be able to physically
see everything break.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.720
That doesn't make it all better,

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.283
that doesn't make it go away,

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.333
but I'm happy with who I am.

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:01.653
(light serene music)

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:11.433
- Be yourself and don't
be scared to be yourself.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:13.421
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new
channel, and now your part.

00:05:13.421 --> 00:05:14.930
- [Both] Subscribe here

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:15.993
- That was my part.

